    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nReproducing mappings in Insert mode with present multicursor changes the value of `[count]`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create the following `init.lua`:\n\n    ```lua\n    local rhs = function() return (vim.v.count > 0 and vim.v.count or '') .. 'Hello' end\n    vim.keymap.set('i', 'xx', rhs, { expr = true })\n    -- For easier repro\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, false, { '', '' })\n    ```\n\n2. `nvim --clean -u init.lua`\n3. `Qj` to initialize multicursor, `i` to start Insert mode.\n4. `xx` - inserts `1Hello` at both cursors. Typing this without active multicursor correctly inserts just `Hello`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nPresence of multicursor has not effect on `[count]` value in any mode.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1929+g17f43325b1\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.2.11-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage",
